Class definition and implementation
-----------------------------------

class Classname : Parent
	
	type membername
	
	[type,...] methodname([type [argname],...])
	
end

impl Classname

	type privatemembername
	
	[type,type...] methodname(type argname,...)
		
	end
end

Expression (anything that has a value)
======================================

Constants: numbers, strings
Identifiers
Constructors: array, vector, pack
Method call: exp binop exp, unop exp, exp[exp], exp.name(explist), exp name exp ("binop"), name exp ("unop")
Member access: exp.name
Parens: ( exp )

[ Distinction between names and operators for infix and prefix calls is done only at lexing. This way, builtin operators can be separated from names, and it allows spaceless calls like a*b. But then treated equivalently by the parser.]

Statement (anything that may not have a value, found in a method)
=================================================================

Lone method call
Assignment: lvaluelist = explist
Control structures: if, while, for, etc.
Return

Left value (anything that can be left of an assignment)
=======================================================

Identifiers
Writable index method call: name[exp]
Member access: name.name
